{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f1387209d0881631","name":"Cockpit Ejection System","source":{"id":"source:reference-f1387209d0881631","title":"Cockpit Ejection System","revision":19628,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:18:59Z","sha256":"d2cead3f7b7ead80fffd0b0c85cb074ad34242c1a311305b133e34b4bd914f27","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19628","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Cockpit%20Ejection%20System&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f1387209d0881631","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Emplacement Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emplacement_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size Restriction:"]}," Gargantuan or Colossal\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 8,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A popular modification for tramp freighters and bounty hunter ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", a Cockpit Ejection System allows a ship's cockpit to eject in the event of the ship's destruction, and subsequently act as an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Escape Pod"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Escape_Pod","referenceId":"reference:a257ab4a352c2042"},". When the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," is destroyed, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," makes a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," check. If the check is successful, the cockpit ejects without its inhabitants taking any damage from the destruction of their ship. On a failed check, those within the cockpit take half the damage that exceeds the ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},", as normal, before the cockpit manages to separate.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
